  "title": "Sei Shōnagon",
  "summary": "Sei Shōnagon was a Japanese court lady serving Empress Teishi during the Heian period, renowned for composing The Pillow Book around 1002 CE. Pioneering the zuihitsu genre of witty prose sketches, personal lists, and poetic musings, her keen observations and aesthetic commentary formed a cornerstone of classical Japanese literature alongside the works of her contemporary Murasaki Shikibu.",
